@page "/community"

<Seo Canonical="/community" Title="Blazorise Community License (Obsolete)" Description="Community licensing is closed to new applicants. Existing licenses remain supported under their original terms." />

<Div Class="b-visual b-marketing b-expanded-page">
    <MarketingPageHeader Variant="BrandBackdropVariant.CircleScatter" Counterpoint="BrandBackdropVariant.CircleScatter">
        <Title>Community licensing<br /><Span>is now obsolete.</Span></Title>
        <Description>Community is closed to new applicants. Existing Community licenses remain supported under their original terms.</Description>
        <Actions>
            <Anchor To="indie" Class="b-visual-button b-visual-button-primary">Explore Indie</Anchor>
            <Anchor To="docs/start" Class="b-visual-button b-visual-button-outline">Get started</Anchor>
        </Actions>
    </MarketingPageHeader>
    <Container Padding="Padding.Is5.OnY">
        <Heading Size="HeadingSize.Is2">Existing Community licenses</Heading>
        <Paragraph>
            If you already have a Community license, you can continue using it under its original terms. You do not need to switch to Indie because Community is closed to new applicants.
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>
            Applications using a Community ProductToken continue to display the compact <Strong>Community License</Strong> notice. See the <Anchor To="docs/usage/licensing">licensing guide</Anchor> for token behavior.
        </Paragraph>
        <Heading Size="HeadingSize.Is2">Starting a new project</Heading>
        <Paragraph>
            Professional and Enterprise cover unlimited projects per licensed developer and include dedicated support. For one developer building an independently owned product, <Anchor To="indie">Indie</Anchor> offers annual project licensing subject to its eligibility requirements. Compare <Anchor To="pricing">plans and benefits</Anchor> before purchasing.
        </Paragraph>
    </Container>
</Div>